list.item:
its bounds, always where they can be given, in TEI's attributes, as years of four digits
        (0813), months (0816-08) or days (0813-06-13):


a point known to its precision: when;

a point somewhere between two dates: notBefore and notAfter;

a span, such as a bishop's years or an owner's: from and to;

its EDTF, where the bounds can't say what the words do: in when-custom for a point, in from-custom and to-custom for a span's ends, with datingMethod pointing to the file's declaration of EDTF, #edtf (). EDTF says:
circa, by ~ (0800~), uncertain, by ? (0756?), or both, by %;
a century or a decade, by unspecified digits (08XX, 081X);
a point among a few dates, by a set ([0755,0756]).

the bounds agree with the EDTF, by years: an exact date has the bounds' years; one with unspecified
        digits may differ from them by a year at each end, as a century does; a circa or uncertain one lies within
        the bounds (a warning);
